PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_5pyboy_5pyboy_5PyBoy_20button, "\n        Send input to PyBoy in the form of \"a\", \"b\", \"start\", \"select\", \"left\", \"right\", \"up\" and \"down\".\n\n        The button will automatically be released at the following call to `PyBoy.tick`.\n\n        Example:\n        ```python\n        >>> pyboy.button(\047a\047) # Press button \047a\047 and release after `pyboy.tick()`\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 pressed\n        True\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 released\n        True\n        >>> pyboy.button(\047a\047, 3) # Press button \047a\047 and release after 3 `pyboy.tick()`\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 pressed\n        True\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 still pressed\n        True\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 still pressed\n        True\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 released\n        True\n        ```\n\n        Args:\n            input (str): button to press\n            delay (int, optional): Number of frames to delay the release. Defaults to 1\n        ");
