PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_5pyboy_5pyboy_5PyBoy_22button_press, "\n        Send input to PyBoy in the form of \"a\", \"b\", \"start\", \"select\", \"left\", \"right\", \"up\" and \"down\".\n\n        The button will remain press until explicitly released with `PyBoy.button_release` or `PyBoy.send_input`.\n\n        Example:\n        ```python\n        >>> pyboy.button_press(\047a\047) # Press button \047a\047 and keep pressed after `PyBoy.tick()`\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 pressed\n        True\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 still pressed\n        True\n        >>> pyboy.button_release(\047a\047) # Release button \047a\047 on next call to `PyBoy.tick()`\n        >>> pyboy.tick() # Button \047a\047 released\n        True\n\n        ```\n\n        Args:\n            input (str): button to press\n        ");
